## 2. Confirmed Requirements

### Functional Requirements
- FR1: Accept a document via file upload (PDF/TXT), pasted text, or a public URL
- FR2: Enforce a 5MB / ~25-page limit on ingested documents
- FR3: Optionally accept a "document context" (relationship to document, or focus area)
- FR4: Produce a whole-document summary (type, parties if extractable, plain summary, key obligations, key dates, key financial terms)
- FR5: Produce a clause-by-clause breakdown, each tagged with a review label, "what it says," "in plain language," "why it may matter," and "questions to consider," with a section/page reference — rendered as **Clause Cards**
- FR6: Answer free-text questions grounded strictly in the uploaded document, with citations, and explicitly say when something isn't covered
- FR7: Generate an exportable Review Checklist (Markdown/TXT, PDF, copy-to-clipboard)
- FR8: Accept two documents and produce a comparison: overview, structured difference table, detailed clause-level comparison, using non-judgmental diff categories
- FR9: Never persist raw uploaded document content beyond the active session

### Non-Functional Requirements
- NFR1: Runs entirely on free-tier infrastructure (LLM, embeddings, hosting)
- NFR2: Deployable as a single publicly reachable URL
- NFR3: Privacy-first: no document persistence by default, no logging of document content
- NFR4: Graceful degradation on LLM/parsing failures (never a raw stack trace to the user)
- NFR5: Reasonable responsiveness for a live demo (processing states must reflect real progress, not spin indefinitely with no feedback)
- NFR6: LangGraph orchestrates all multi-agent pipelines; the graph is the single source of truth for workflow progression

### Assumptions
- OpenRouter's free-tier models remain available and usable throughout the 10-day build and judging window
- HuggingFace sentence-transformer embedding models run within Streamlit Community Cloud's RAM limits (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2` is ~90 MB, acceptable)
- FAISS (CPU) indexing is fast enough on session-scoped, small document sizes
- Streamlit Community Cloud's free-tier resources are sufficient for this workload

### Constraints
- 10-day solo build timeline
- Free-tier services only, no paid infrastructure
- Separate `frontend/` and `backend/` directories within a single deployable Streamlit service

