## 4. Architecture Decision: LangGraph as Orchestration Layer

### Why LangGraph?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is the core architectural change from v1. LangGraph replaces ad-hoc service-call chains with a **stateful, directed graph** that makes each processing step explicit, observable, and recoverable.

**Benefits:**
- Each node in the graph is a discrete, testable unit (ingest → index → extract_clauses → build_cards → summarize → done)
- Graph state is typed (TypedDict/Pydantic) — the UI can subscribe to state updates and render staged progress accurately
- Retry and conditional branching (e.g., "if PDF → use page-index path; else → use FAISS path") are first-class graph edges, not buried `if/else` blocks
- Agents (ClauseExtractor, CardBuilder, Summarizer, QAAgent) can be composed, reordered, or swapped without touching the UI
- Makes it straightforward to add streaming/intermediate output in the future

### LangGraph Graph Design

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    START([START]) --> InputRouter

    InputRouter -->|PDF| PDFIngestNode
    InputRouter -->|URL| URLIngestNode
    InputRouter -->|Text| TextIngestNode

    PDFIngestNode --> PDFIndexNode["PDFIndexNode (page-tree index, vectorless)"]
    URLIngestNode --> URLEmbedNode["URLEmbedNode (scrape, chunk, FAISS + HF embed)"]
    TextIngestNode --> TextEmbedNode["TextEmbedNode (chunk, FAISS + HF embed)"]

    PDFIndexNode --> ClauseExtractAgent
    URLEmbedNode --> ClauseExtractAgent
    TextEmbedNode --> ClauseExtractAgent

    ClauseExtractAgent --> CardBuilderAgent
    CardBuilderAgent --> SummaryAgent
    SummaryAgent --> END([END / Results Ready])

    ClauseExtractAgent -->|Extraction failed| RetryNode
    RetryNode --> ClauseExtractAgent
    RetryNode -->|Max retries| DegradedClauseNode["Mark clause Unclear"]
    DegradedClauseNode --> CardBuilderAgent
```

### Retrieval Strategy by Input Type

| Input Type | Index Strategy | Embedding | RAG Type |
|---|---|---|---|
| **PDF** | Per-page tree index; each page is a node keyed by page number | None (vectorless) | Structured clause list passed directly as LLM context; BM25 fallback for very long docs |
| **URL** | Scrape with `trafilatura`, chunk, FAISS `.index` in `session_state` | HuggingFace `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (free, local) | Semantic FAISS retrieval on user question or clause-extraction query |
| **Text (paste)** | Chunk, FAISS `.index` in `session_state` | HuggingFace `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (free, local) | Semantic FAISS retrieval on user question or clause-extraction query |

**Key design decision:** PDF gets vectorless RAG because page boundaries give us natural structure and reliable citation. URL/text get FAISS because they lack inherent structure — semantic search is needed to find relevant chunks for clause extraction and Q&A.

