## 9. Clause Card Design

The **Clause Card** is the primary output unit of ClearClause. Each card is generated by the `CardBuilderAgent` and rendered by `frontend/ui/clause_card.py`.

### Clause Card Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `title` | `str` | Short, plain-English title for the clause (e.g., "Early Termination Fee") |
| `plain_meaning` | `str` | What the clause actually means, in one plain sentence |
| `priority` | `Literal["High", "Medium", "Low", "FYI"]` | How urgently the reader should engage with this clause |
| `questions_to_ask` | `list[str]` | 2–4 concrete questions the reader should ask before signing |
| `review_label` | `str` | One of: Review carefully / Potentially important / Standard / Beneficial / Unclear |
| `section_reference` | `str` | Page number (PDF) or chunk index (URL/text) |
| `original_text` | `str` | Verbatim clause text |

### Priority Mapping

| Priority | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **High** | Significant financial or legal consequence; warrants professional advice |
| **Medium** | Affects your rights or obligations in a meaningful way |
| **Low** | Standard clause, unlikely to cause issues, but worth knowing |
| **FYI** | Informational; no action usually needed |

