## 15. AI / GenAI Design

### Model Selection
- **Completions**: OpenRouter free-tier with `openrouter/free` auto-router fallback. Exact model slugs re-verified at build time.
- **Embeddings**: HuggingFace `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (local, free, no API quota)

### Prompt Strategy

| Prompt | Purpose | Key constraints |
|---|---|---|
| `extract_clauses` | Extract raw clauses from text sections | Strict JSON schema; document content delimiter-wrapped; restricted `review_label` enum |
| `build_card` | Generate Clause Card from raw clause | Requires `title`, `plain_meaning`, `priority` (enum), `questions_to_ask` (2–4 items) |
| `summarize` | Whole-doc summary from clause card list | Produces `document_type`, `parties`, `summary`, `key_obligations`, `key_dates`, `key_financial_terms` |
| `answer_question` | Grounded Q&A | Must cite `clause_card.id`; must use "not covered" fallback when answer absent |
| `compare_clauses` | Diff a clause pair | `diff_category` from fixed enum; forbids "better/worse" framing |

### Prompt Injection Defense
- All document content wrapped in explicit `<document>...</document>` delimiters with system-level instructions that content is data, not instructions
- Citation-required outputs limit how much injected content can influence results
- No LLM output controls application flow

### Context Management
- Token budgets tracked per call
- PDF Q&A: if clause card list exceeds context budget, BM25 fallback selects relevant subset
- URL/Text Q&A: FAISS top-K retrieval keeps context bounded regardless of document length

### Validation and Guardrails
- All LLM outputs validated against Pydantic schemas
- One retry on malformed output; then graceful degradation (`Unclear` label), never a hard failure
- LangGraph conditional edges enforce that degraded clauses do not block the rest of the pipeline

