## 16. Security Design

| Threat | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| **Prompt injection** | Document content wrapped in `<document>` delimiters; system instructions declare it as untrusted data; citation-required outputs; no LLM output controls app flow |
| **SSRF via URL input** | HTTPS-only enforcement; 10s timeout; response size cap (5 MB); block requests to private/loopback IP ranges (127.x, 10.x, 192.168.x, 169.254.x) |
| **Malicious PDF** | PyMuPDF parsing wrapped in try/except; no JavaScript execution; no external resource loading from PDF |
| **Oversized uploads** | 5 MB enforced client-side (Streamlit) and server-side (pre-parse check) |
| **API key exposure** | Keys stored in Streamlit Cloud secrets manager / local `secrets.toml` (gitignored); `.env.example` has placeholder values only |
| **Document content in logs** | Only metadata logged (size, duration, error type — never raw text or full prompts) |
| **Rate limiting** | Per-session request counter in `session_state`; blocks excessive LLM calls during demo load |
| **Dependency vulnerabilities** | GitHub Dependabot enabled for automatic vulnerability alerts |
| **Transport security** | HTTPS handled by Streamlit Community Cloud automatically |
| **Session isolation** | FAISS index and all document data stored in `session_state`; no cross-session sharing possible |

